## Home Assistant requires custom cards to be built using standard browser Web Components. The core lifecycle handles the state orchestration entirely:

- setConfig(config): Called once when the card loads or when the YAML configuration changes. You use this to store your card's user settings.set
- hass(hass): Called continuously by Home Assistant whenever any state in the system changes. This is where your card updates its internal tracking and triggers UI re-renders.
- fireEvent: To execute actions, your card dispatches a standard DOM event (hass-action or a call-service request), which Home Assistant intercepts to handle the backend processing.

## CARD BASICS

1. Editor Experience

- The Editor will have the following configurable options:
  - Title
  - Subtitle
  - Content (markup)
- Editor will use default Home Assistant components such as <ha-input> over regular <input>. If the Home Assistant components are not able to be used, then the resulting formatting should mimick the Home Assistant Component (https://design.home-assistant.io/#concepts/home)

